WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:10.510
[blues piano]

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:14.614
DINAH WASHINGTON (Singing):
What a difference a day made.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:33.133
24 little hours Brought
the sun and the flowers

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.336
where there used to be rain!

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.743
My yesterday was blue, dear.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.981
C.L. FRANKLIN: Come on down
here and join the party.

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:49.249
Come on.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.617
DINAH WASHINGTON (Singing):
Today I'm a part of you, dear.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:51.718
C.L. FRANKLIN: Ha, ha!

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:52.752
That's my girl.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.623
DINAH WASHINGTON
(Singing): My lonely nights

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.791
are through, dear.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.431
Since you said, you were mine.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:11.304
Lord, what a
difference a day makes.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.878
There's a rainbow before me.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:25.585
The skies above can't be stormy.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.624
TED WHITE: And which one of
C.L.'s daughters is this?

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.759
ARETHA FRANKLIN:
I'm Aretha Louise.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.195
TED WHITE: Well, nice
to meet you, Aretha.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.363
I'm Ted White.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.232
DINAH WASHINGTON
(Singing): It's heaven when

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:46.639
you find romance on your menu.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:02:00.553
What a difference a day made,
and the difference is you.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:10.363
[applause, cheering]

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.731
DINAH WASHINGTON: Thank you.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:12.465
I'mma record that one.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.666
TED WHITE: Yeah, you better.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.269
C.L. FRANKLIN: My
daughter, Aretha.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.403
BARBARA SIGGERS
FRANKLIN: Oh, C.L.,

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.706
don't make Ree sing if
she doesn't want to.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.242
C.L. FRANKLIN: Ree
listens to the radio.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:26.312
She can hear any song and
sing it back note for note.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:32.819
And tonight, we got a bona
fide radio star in our house.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.788
So, so how would you all like
to hear a little sing along?

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:39.759
A little call and response?

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.760
Hey?

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:41.861
TED WHITE: What, is it
like a little parlor

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:42.862
trick or something like that?

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.097
BARBARA SIGGERS FRANKLIN: No.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.365
Little Ree's good.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.037
DINAH WASHINGTON
(Singing): Did you

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:54.240
say I've got a lot to learn?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.848
ARETHA FRANKLIN
(Singing): Did you

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:06.152
say I've got a lot to learn?

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:11.057
[cheering]

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.258
DINAH WASHINGTON
(Singing): Since this

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.194
is the perfect spot to learn,

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.463
DINAH AND ARETHA TOGETHER:
Teach me tonight.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.902
TED WHITE: Ha ha!

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.871
Did you see that?

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.172
You got something there.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.307
C.L. FRANKLIN: That's it!

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.841
DINAH WASHINGTON: Ree's
gonna be the next great one.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:29.742
C.L. FRANKLIN: Yes she is.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.245
Yes, she is.

